# Practical 4:  Connecting TikTok Frontend to Backend

## What I Built

For this practical I built the frontend for a TikTok clone using Next.js and Tailwind CSS. I connected it to the Express.js backend I built separately, implementing user authentication, a scrolling video feed, video uploads, a follow system, user profiles, and an explore page. The UI closely matches the real TikTok layout — sidebar navigation, vertical video cards with action buttons, and a modal-based login/signup flow.

---

## Tech Stack

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Next.js 16 (App Router) | React framework with file-based routing |
| Tailwind CSS | Utility-first styling |
| Axios | HTTP requests to the backend API |
| React Context API | Global authentication state |
| Intersection Observer API | Auto play/pause videos on scroll |
| jwt-decode | Decoding JWT tokens on the client |
| react-hot-toast | Toast notifications |

---

